  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Autonomous peer — local scope",
      "items": [
        "Each repository retains local authority and judgment. Exchange scoped claims, artifacts and conformance, never permission. Small capability contracts grow an interchangeable ecosystem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Admission and result are different claims",
      "items": [
        "All required inputs: Authorized subject; Applicable authority; Compiled Commitment; Fresh observations; TransitionPlan; Integrated candidate; Local executed claim.",
        "Required claim selector: all declared proof-plane claims whose exact subject, predicate, scope, bindings, validity and verifier apply.",
        "Attestation is the sole durable semantic result, scoped by predicate, bindings, validity and verifier, never permission. Commitment, Facts and Plan are transient. Change relations and experiments are derived: no persistent workflow graph, compatibility residue, feedback ledger or memory-backed truth.",
        "Own candidate, policy, fresh authority and proof belong to this repository. Shared admission grammar does not import the ETHOS accepted root, another repository’s objects or its permission."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Refusal and uncertainty are different",
      "items": [
        "A stale effect-time check admits no runner. A definite CAS mismatch means this local CAS did not update its ref; it does not undo earlier effects or other resources. An uncertain outcome must be observed before any further attempt.",
        "Contradiction or missing meaning blocks the affected effect. Preserve the counterexample, promote the smallest model boundary and recompile; no exception route around authority."
      ]
    }
  ]
